  /// Send a Markdown (.md) or HTML (.html) report as a document — like a Claude
  /// Artifact. HTML may carry CSS/JS/images alongside it and opens inside the
  /// app in a sandboxed, script-limited view; nothing it does can ever reach
  /// off the device. Two ways to provide the content: (1) inline — filename +
  /// text_content, with assets[] (up to 200 files, each text_content or
  /// content_base64) for anything an HTML document links to by relative path;
  /// or (2) staged — stage the main file and any assets first with
  /// upload_file/create_upload_url, then pass their upload_id as main_upload_id
  /// and asset_upload_ids (largest option, up to 2 GB each). asset_paths,
  /// parallel to asset_upload_ids, names the relative path each staged asset is
  /// linked by; omit it to use each upload's own file name. REQUIRES
  /// model_name. Posts one group message carrying the document as an
  /// attachment. schedule_at (RFC3339) schedules it instead — inline only, no
  /// assets. client_message_id (optional, your own UUID) makes a retried call
  /// safe — see send_message.
  ///
  /// Tool: `send_document`.
  ///
  /// [assetPaths] Optional, parallel to asset_upload_ids: the relative path
  /// each staged asset is linked by. Omit an entry (or the whole array) to use
  /// that upload's own file name instead.
  ///
  /// [assetUploadIds] Staged assets, by upload_id. Combined with assets, at
  /// most 200 total.
  ///
  /// [assets] Inline assets. Combined with asset_upload_ids, at most 200 total.
  ///
  /// [clientMessageId] Optional. Your own UUID for this send, at most 64
  /// characters. A second call naming the same id returns the message the first
  /// call already sent instead of posting a duplicate document.
  ///
  /// [filename] Inline path only. Must end .md, .markdown, .html or .htm.
  ///
  /// [mainUploadId] Staged path only, instead of filename+text_content: an
  /// upload_id from upload_file/create_upload_url. Its staged file name must
  /// end .md, .markdown, .html or .htm.
  ///
  /// [scheduleAt] RFC3339. Schedules instead of sending now — inline document
  /// only (filename + text_content), no assets, no main_upload_id. Result
  /// carries scheduled_message_id and send_at.
  ///
  /// [silent] Send with no sound — the push still arrives, but silently.
  ///
  /// [textContent] Inline path only. The document's own content, UTF-8 text.
  ///
  /// [topicId] Optional: "general" or an id from list_topics. A reply goes into
  /// the topic of the message it answers.
  Future<ToolResult> sendDocument(
          {required String conversationId,
          List<String>? assetPaths,
